%description:

TcpSpoof.isSYN:true-no-tcp -- the SYN-ACK comes back as Protocol Unreachable, and the listener closes the forked connection.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sends fabricated TCP packets. ... Compatible with both IPv4
(~Ipv4) and IPv6 (~Ipv6)." TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sends one segment at the time t: a
header of 20 bytes without options and data, with the window 16384, no ACK, and the SYN bit
of isSYN.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Whether to set the SYN bit on the packet".

The classes: true (the default: the segment is a SYN) and false (the segment has no
control bit at all). The code: TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sets the SYN bit from the value,
and no other bit. The facet true-no-tcp: the node of the spoof has no TCP, so its IP answers the SYN-ACK of a
listener with an ICMP Destination Unreachable, Protocol Unreachable (3/2), which is a hard
error (RFC 9293 section 3.9.2.2). The listener of host2 forks a connection for the SYN, and
that connection closes at the error. Its application has no socket for the connection before
it accepts it, so it gets no indication (RFC 9293 section 3.10.7.3: "The user need not be
informed"). This test separates "true" from "false", where the listener sends no SYN-ACK.

Node under test: host1; host1 has TcpSpoof in place of its TCP and no application; host2
listens at the port 1000 (TcpEchoApp). The spoof sends one SYN at 1 s from the port 5000 to
host2:1000 with the sequence number 12345. Observation: level 1, host1 answers the SYN-ACK of
host2 with the ICMP error, and host2 sends no segment in the next 3 s, in which its timer
would send the SYN-ACK again; the run ends without an error.

%# parameter: TcpSpoof.isSYN
%# class: true-no-tcp
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.isSYN
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueNoTcp")
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 5000 && tcp.synBit == true")
             .describe("the SYN of the spoof")
             .within(1.1))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.ackNo == 12346")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of host2")
             .within(0.1))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("icmpv4.type == 3 && icmpv4.code == 2")
             .describe("the Protocol Unreachable of host1")
             .within(0.1))
        .never(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 1000")
              .describe("a segment of host2 after the error")
              .within(3.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueNoTcp compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.typename = "TcpSpoof"
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host1.tcp.srcAddress = ""
*.host1.tcp.destAddress = "host2"
*.host1.tcp.srcPort = 5000
*.host1.tcp.destPort = 1000
*.host1.tcp.seqNo = 12345
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true
*.host1.tcp.t = 1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSpoofIsSYNTrueNoTcp: PASS
